    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> republic between the Orange and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaal-river">Vaal</a> rivers, recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein-convention">Bloemfontein Convention</a> of 1854.</li><li>Its orderly constitution and long presidency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-brand">Johannes Brand</a> earned it the name of a model republic.</li><li>Wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a> won it fertile land, but its alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> led to its conquest in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> took the diamond fields of Griqualand West in 1871, the Free State settled the quarrel peacefully: President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-brand">Brand</a> accepted £90,000 in compensation in 1876.</p></aside>
    </section>

